  "branch": "codex/require-service-owned-data-roots",
  "title": "Require service-owned data roots independently of Git layout",
  "body": "The resolver rejected a services section when it was its own Git checkout, while accepting arbitrary roots outside a checkout. Require the selected existing real services section above data/, refuse home .local, installed-code and symlink-backed data roots, and keep config/environment/argv precedence and the immutable result. Applications use their existing explicit owner selection.\n\nVersion 0.3.0 marks the intentional change to formerly admitted app/arbitrary roots. All four source test families pass: 49 tests, no failures or skips. The five curated records include independent source receiving, exact base/parent identities, named native observations and preserved earlier test failures; raw captures stay in owned logs.\n\nThis is source-only integration. The shared npm runner/dependency closure, package publication, CSE dependency update, deployed explicit owner bindings and actual federation use remain unreceived. CDE ownerDataRoot takes section/data; this resolver returns the section above data. No installed or live-host change is claimed.",
  "commitMessage": "Require service-owned process data roots\n\nReplace Git-topology ownership with received canonical section paths.\nKeep explicit config precedence and process boundary contracts.\nReceive all four source Node test families and scoped source review.\nRegistry, CSE dependency and host owner-binding uptake remain separate.\n",
